  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your Matadors! Since they can clear any blocked arm, they are your only way to save a round when the table is filled with cards that have no 'Seven' matches left. Don't waste them early.\n\nSuit Control: Try to hold two strong suits that total to seven, such as the 2s and the 5s. This gives you flexibility in playing regular tiles. Watch the blanksâ€”once an arm ends in 0, only a Matador can extend it.\n\nThe Zero Strategy: The 0-0 Matador is the most dangerous tile. If you play it across an arm, the next player MUST play another Matador to continue it. Use this to force your opponent to use their best tiles prematurely. Offensive Drawing: If you have a clear lead, don't be afraid to draw from the boneyard even if you have a play, as long as the boneyard is large. This 'starves' the opponent of Matadors hidden in the stock.",
    Player: "Keep your Matadors! Since they can clear any blocked arm, they are your only way to save a round when the table is filled with cards that have no 'Seven' matches left. Don't waste them early.\n\nSuit Control: Try to hold two strong suits that total to seven, such as the 2s and the 5s. This gives you flexibility in playing regular tiles. Watch the blanksâ€”once an arm ends in 0, only a Matador can extend it.\n\nThe Zero Strategy: The 0-0 Matador is the most dangerous tile. If you play it across an arm, the next player MUST play another Matador to continue it. Use this to force your opponent to use their best tiles prematurely. Offensive Drawing: If you have a clear lead, don't be afraid to draw from the boneyard even if you have a play, as long as the boneyard is large. This 'starves' the opponent of Matadors hidden in the stock.",
